{
  "_comment": [
    "Fragua HMI tag list — the PLC_PRG points the FRAGUAV3 Perspective views",
    "bind to ([default]PLC_PRG/*). This is what makes the existing HMI panel",
    "— low / med / HVAC / Luces / Charts / Alarms — light up without editing",
    "a single view.",
    "",
    "Companion to fragua-tags.json, which carries the 25-point site schedule",
    "that feeds the EmberNet dashboard. Both sets run in the same EmberBurn",
    "instance; this one is additionally exposed over OPC-UA on :4840 for",
    "Ignition Edge to import into its [default] provider.",
    "",
    "Data, not configuration: pushed in with seed-tags.py and persisted by",
    "EmberBurn to its own volume. Nothing here is in a chart or an image.",
    "",
    "The model is a plant, not noise: compressors and HVAC units run under",
    "hysteresis control off their own space temperature, so the rooms hold",
    "setpoint and the run status agrees with the temperature; control output",
    "modulates with deviation and is zero when the unit is stopped; each",
    "load's kW derives from what that load is doing; KW is the sum of them",
    "plus base load; KVA and KVAR come off the power triangle; and KWH and",
    "KVARH integrate their own source rather than ticking at a fixed rate."
  ],
